==Battleground==
*250 [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Zuche]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Mega Baa Baa]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Daboo of the Dead]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Mega Baa Baa]] spawns after 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>.
**2 [[Deathshund]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
**6 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**4 [[Zuche]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**2 [[Oldhorn]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
**2 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Mega Baa Baa]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
It's actually quite difficult to get a good stalling setup for the Zombies. Wait until Zuche is about to reach the Cat Base, send out [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] to force him to burrow, then [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]]/[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] to catch him while he's unburrowing. Use [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cats]] to shut down Sir Rel, where they will force the second Zuche to burrow. Catch him with another Cat Chief/Cadaver BearCat, kill the second Sir Rel, then let all of your units die to Mega Baa Baa before using your Cat Cannon to clear the field.

This will leave just the 250 Zoges, who you can actually just kill by chucking rocks and using your Cat Cannon once in a while. Do this until you max out your wallet, then, go on the offensive. Start sending out [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cats]], Cat Chiefs/Cadaver BearCats, Royal Guard Cats, etc. Make sure your units all reach the enemy base at the same time. As soon as Daboo of the Dead comes out, time [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] so that he reaches Daboo just as he finishes his attack animation. He'll trade hits with Mega Baa Baa, then move on to beating up Daboo alongside the rest of the army you've built up. Use the Cat Cannon as soon as Deathshund resurfaces, then try to finish him off via Z-Kill.

You can't unburrow any of the Zang Roos without Holy Blast, so do your best to retain as much ground from them as humanly possible (it doesn't really matter if you Z-Kill them, so using generalist attackers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] is fine) whilst your Royal Guard Cats handle the Oldhorns and Sir Rels. Once the second Zang Roo appears and burrows, you can catch her when she resurfaces using Awakened Bahamut Cat, who should be off cooldown by that point. Kill her, then use the Cat Cannon on the second Deathshund when he eventually also pops back up from the ground. You won't get the opportunity to try and Z-Kill him, since Oldhorn will interrupt you, forcing you to deal with him first. However, the biggest threats will be well out of the way by now, so it's just leisurely Royal Guard Cat stacking until either he dies or the Cat Cannon finishes him off (and kills Deathshund). None of the threats can really do anything anymore on their own, so deal with the reviving enemies however you want.

